From: DotRedstone <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boot: preserve menu frame before starting selected entry

Diagnostic only: isolate whether the final systemd-boot ClearScreen call is
responsible for Sheng's one-frame flash after selecting NixOS. The menu's
normal drawing and error handling remain unchanged.

--- a/src/boot/boot.c
+++ b/src/boot/boot.c
@@ -1003,3 +1003,2 @@ static bool menu_run(
         *chosen_entry = config->entries[idx_highlight];
-        clear_screen(COLOR_NORMAL);
         return action == ACTION_RUN;
